* The Metamorph Device in the gene splicer room (openc2e Creatures 2 project,
* our own script). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder);
* safe to repeat.
*
* The device (3 10 13, from the C2 Life Kit's "Metamorphosis device.cob")
* is built into every world from the player's own COB (builtin-cobs.txt),
* which makes it at its own spot east of the lab (7238,1982). The owner
* (2026-11-19) wanted it in another place, and its two versions as one
* device: this moves it to the gene splicer room's floor, between the
* teleporter (x 6145-6229) and the tall pillar with the threaded rod (x
* 6464): 216 px wide, its base on the floor at y 1788 (picture:
* metamorph-lab-mockup.png in the project folder). Built-in objects are made
* anew at each load, so this runs each time; a second device (from the
* Agent Injector) is removed, keeping one.
*
* What it does: a creature in its cabin is replaced by a newly hatched copy
* of the opposite sex, from its own genome with the usual small mutations
* (NEW: GENE of one creature). The two versions in the COB differ only in
* how the creature put in ends: one fills it with five poisons (heavy
* metals, cyanide, belladonna, geddonase and glycotoxin; it is let out and
* dies of them), the other ends it at once. Here OV10 picks: 0 at once
* (the default), 1 the poisons.
*
* Only the hand runs it (2026-11-19): it ends the creature inside, and
* creatures press things often, so a creature's press does nothing.
*
* The switch (2 1 164, sprite zmsw, our own art from
* art/metamorph_lever.py; owner chose the design from mock-ups, 2026-11-19):
* a small riveted plate on the front of the device's left end block, a
* lightning bolt above (at once) and a skull below (poisons), the lever
* pointing at the one in use (picture 0 up, 1 down). A click from the hand
* flips it and sets the device's OV10, with a click sound and no window (the
* owner, 2026-11-19, tried a note window and did not want one). Creatures
* do not see it. It is
* kept with the world (OV99 7461), so its setting stays between launches.
enum 3 10 13
  doif va00 eq 0
    setv va00 targ
  else
    dpas
    kill targ
  endi
next
doif va00 ne 0
  targ va00
  mvto 6244 1601
  doif totl 2 1 164 eq 0
    inst
    new: simp zmsw 2 0 1200 0
    setv cls2 2 1 164
    setv attr 20
    setv ov99 7461
    pose 0
    slow
  endi
* (on the left end block's front face; the device's setting from it)
  setv va01 0
  enum 2 1 164
    mvto 6247 1740
* (a click from the hand sends activate 1; set at each load, as a kept
* object's click setting is not saved)
    bhvr 1 0
    setv va01 pose
  next
  targ va00
  setv ov10 va01
endi

scrp 2 1 164 1
  doif from ne pntr
    setv actv 0
    stop
  endi
  inst
  doif pose eq 0
    pose 1
  else
    pose 0
  endi
  setv var0 pose
  enum 3 10 13
    setv ov10 var0
  next
  snde tick
  targ ownr
  setv actv 0
endm

scrp 3 10 13 1
  doif from ne pntr
    setv actv 0
    stop
  endi
* (not to be cut off midway: the creature would be ended with no copy)
  lock
  sndc bt1_
  gpas
  part 1
  anim [0123456] over
  anim [56R]
  setv var0 0
  etch 4 0 0
    doif movs eq 3 setv var0 targ endi
  next
  doif var0 ne 0
    setv var5 ov10
    targ var0
    aslp 1
* (the copy is the other sex: SPCS 1 male, 2 female)
    setv var1 spcs
    doif var1 eq 1 setv var1 2 else setv var1 1 endi
    setv var2 monk
    setv var3 posx
    setv var4 posy
    doif var5 eq 1
      chem 140 255 chem 141 255 chem 143 255 chem 144 255 chem 145 255
    else
      kill targ
    endi
    wait 30
    inst
    new: gene var2 var2 var9
    new: crea var9 var1
    drea 1
    mvto var3 var4
    slim
    setv grav 1
    targ ownr
    slow
  endi
  part 1
  anim [6543210] over
  wait 5
  dpas
  setv actv 0
endm
